  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 205 PM EDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\n- Tranquil and Relatively Warm This Week\n\nMinimal weather concerns this week as there will be a tendency \nfor high pressure over the Great Lakes region and beyond much of \nthe time. A very El-Nino-looking split upper level jet is over \nNorth America this week, and Michigan will be under weak flow \nthrough Wednesday.\n\nHigh temperatures will generally reside in the mid to upper 60s \nwhile the 30-year normal highs slip into the upper 50s. With the \nmostly clear skies and light winds, nightly lows will be closer to\nnormal, between the mid 30s and mid 40s. Areas of fog Tuesday \nmorning and Wednesday morning are possible. After today, all \nensemble members are very light on winds, until there is just a \nminor uptick Thursday and and into the weekend when a couple of \nweak troughs ripple through the pattern. The lack of moisture and \nlift wouldn't favor much more than a chance of sprinkles.",
